--[[
  VEREUS (F3X) v22

  New in v22:
    - The black smoke particles on the hands are REMOVED (code deleted).
    - Switches at the top if you also want to turn off other effects:
        E_WHITE_EFFECT = false  -> no white flash / white shards on the E blocks
        T_RINGS        = false  -> no dark rings during the T charge and explosion

  VEREUS (F3X) v21

  FIX in v21 (script could fail to load / hang):
    - The T / E effect parts (about 200 parts) used to be created at load,
      which can overload F3X and make the whole script look broken. Now only
      the Vereus model (11 parts) is created at load, and the effects are
      created the first time you press T or E (a short "Preparing the
      effects..." message, then the attack starts by itself).
    - The effect parts are no longer renamed one by one (about 200 fewer
      remote calls) and the ring pool is 60.
    - This version was run through a Roblox simulator in testing (load,
      walking, T, E, X, Z, respawn): no errors.

  VEREUS (F3X) v20

  New in v20:
    - The E blocks are narrow again (9 x 9, like the original) and stand in
      two long rows toward your target. There are 60 of them.
    - Speed is the original's again: WALK_SPEED 92, Z skin 155.
    - Black particles: F3X's smoke decoration is added (black) around the
      hands and orbs, like the original's black particles. If the game's
      F3X does not support it, the script says so in the console (F9) and
      skips it. Turn it off with HAND_PARTICLES = false.

  VEREUS (F3X) v19

  New in v19 (E white effect, matched to your video of the original):
    - When the blocks appear, they now burst out dense, spiky WHITE shards
      that fly outward and lie tilted over the ground, like the starburst in
      the original. The blocks near you make 4 shards each (random tilt and
      spin, up to ~230 studs wide); far blocks make 1.
    - The ring pool is 90 parts so the burst is not cut short.

  VEREUS (F3X) v18

  New in v18 (E):
    - The rows are always full length (about 700 studs), no matter how close
      you tap, so E makes a LONG line.
    - Every block is now a long wall piece (about 30 studs long along the
      row, 9 wide, 50-80 tall) turned along the row, so the pieces join
      into long continuous walls instead of separate thin pillars. The
      height stays moderate.

  VEREUS (F3X) v17

  New in v17:
    - Slower walking: WALK_SPEED is 40 (the original is 92) and the Z skin
      is 70 (the original 155). Change them at the top if you want.
    - Less lag during T and E: fewer rings are created (the ring pool is
      70 instead of 110, T charge makes a ring every 0.05 s instead of
      0.03, the explosion every 0.06 s), 50 pillars instead of 60, and the
      effects are sent every 0.14 s (FX_INTERVAL), so the body and hands
      update without waiting for them.

  VEREUS (F3X) v16

  New in v16:
    - E blocks: each one has a different height (50-80 studs, so not tiny
      and not huge) and they stay in two long rows toward your target.
    - Every E block appears with a WHITE flash (bright white for the first
      half second, then it turns dark), plus the white shockwave rings.
    - T works like E: press T, tap where you want to attack during the
      charge (your body keeps turning to your latest tap), and the ball
      flies to your latest tap.

  VEREUS (F3X) v15

  New in v15:
    - E has a pause (E_WIND = 2 seconds) so you can choose the direction:
      press E, then tap where you want to attack. Your body keeps turning
      to your latest tap during the pause. Then the attack goes that way.
    - E boxes (pillars) now stand in TWO LONG ROWS along the line to your
      target (left and right of it), instead of one clump.
    - Shockwave rings last twice as long (RING_SLOW = 2), so the T and E
      effects are slower and last longer, closer to the original.

  VEREUS (F3X) v14

  New in v14 (more effects, like the video):
    - E: 60 pillars instead of 30, packed closer (12 studs apart) and
      spread wider, so they form a wall of towers; the wall stays for about
      6 seconds; every pillar lands with 3 white shockwaves (bigger
      starburst). Pillars wobble less often, so it sends less data.
    - T: twice as many dark rings during the charge, 2 rings around the
      ball at a time, and the explosion makes 4 shockwave rings every 0.04 s
      instead of 2 every 0.06 s. The ring pool is now 70 parts.

  VEREUS (F3X) v13

  New in v13:
    - The red aiming dot is gone. You still aim the same way as in the
      original: tap / click the spot, then press T or E.
    - E and T now last as long as the original script (E about 1.25 + 0.45
      + 1.5 seconds of build-up, pillars stay about 3 seconds; T charges
      for about 4.2 seconds). ATTACK_SPEED is back to 1.

  VEREUS (F3X) v12

  New in v12:
    - E is much quicker: the hands go down and the black boxes (discs)
      appear almost immediately, and the pillars follow right after. The
      whole attack now takes only a couple of seconds.

  VEREUS (F3X) v11

  New in v11:
    - Walk like the original: the whole body bobs, pitches, yaws and leans
      into turns (the original's ROOTLERP), the head sways a little on its
      own, and the third skin (Z) walks the way the original's "xester"
      does (arms low and still, speed 155).
    - Aiming: TAP (or click) where you want to attack, then press T or E.
      A red dot shows your target (only you see it). You turn toward it,
      the T ball flies to it and the E pillars sweep toward it and stop
      there. Without a tap they go straight ahead.
    - E is a lot shorter, ATTACK_SPEED is now 0.85.

  VEREUS (F3X) v10

  New in v10:
    - Skin change (X / Z) now plays the original's transformation: the body
      bows forward, both hands go up beside the head, then a RED (X) or
      WHITE (Z) burst (rings + expanding ball) and the skin swaps. X gives
      black hands, Z gives white hands, like the original.
    - E attack is shorter (pillars land faster, stay shorter).
    - ATTACK_SPEED default is now 0.75.

  VEREUS (F3X) v9

  New in v9:
    - Smoother walking: updates are now sent without waiting for the
      previous one to come back (up to MAX_INFLIGHT at once), so the model
      is updated at the full SEND_RATE instead of once per ping. The
      prediction now uses the full round trip and is smoothed.
    - Slower attacks: ATTACK_SPEED = 0.6 stretches every attack (hand
      movement, pillars, ball) to 60 percent speed. 1 = original speed.

  VEREUS (F3X) v8

  New in v8:
    - E attack rebuilt like the original: a line of black pillars sweeps
      away from you (about 700 studs), each one swings down from above,
      lands with a white shockwave, wobbles, then sinks away. Black discs
      stay on the ground and spread out at the end. VISUAL ONLY.
    - AVATAR_MODE = "invisible": F3X is asked to make your real avatar
      transparent on the server so everyone sees you invisible. If the game
      refuses, it falls back to hiding the avatar only for you.

  VEREUS (F3X) v7

  New in v7:
    - E = the original's "black pillars" attack: the hands go up, then flat
      black discs appear on the ground in front of you and tall black
      pillars shoot up from them. VISUAL ONLY.
    - X = second skin (grey horns / mask), Z = third skin (the red-black
      jester). Press the same key again to go back to the normal skin.
    - Your avatar turns black (AVATAR_MODE = "black"; "hide" makes it
      invisible). Only you see this change.
    - On-screen buttons for T, E, X and Z.

  IMPORTANT: none of the attacks hurt, kill, push or touch other players.
  F3X can only build and move parts, and this script does not add damage.

  VEREUS (F3X) v6

  BUG FIX in v6 (the black glossy ball / eye floating away from the head):
    - The update loop shared one list with the effect parts, so poses could
      be matched to the wrong parts. They are now matched by index.
    - A health check runs every second: if any part drifted away or became
      unanchored, it is put back (and its name is printed in the console).
    - Parts of an older copy left behind near you are removed on load.

  VEREUS (F3X) v5

  New in v5 (the T attack is now much closer to the original):
    - Ground: two layers of big dark rings (up to the original's 310 / 241
      studs) are spawned continuously while you charge, plus thin dark rings
      flashing around the black ball.
    - Ball speed is the original's 300 studs/second.
    - Explosion: the black ball grows with the original's curve (about 955
      studs) and fades, while two kinds of dark shockwave rings (flat and
      TALL shards) keep spawning, like the sky full of dark shards in the
      original.
    - Still VISUAL ONLY: it never hurts, pushes or touches other players.

  New in v4:
    - T now plays the ORIGINAL Vereus energy-ball attack, like your video:
      both hands go into the charge pose, a black ball grows in front of the
      hand while dark rings spread over the ground, then the ball is thrown
      and explodes into a huge black blast with dark pillars.
      It is VISUAL ONLY: it never hurts, pushes or touches other players.
    - You can't walk while charging (like the original).
    - An ATTACK button is shown on screen (handy on mobile).
    - E is still the hand slam from v3.
    - Everything from v3 is kept: loads only when you execute, nothing
      reloads after a reset, original speed 92, clean re-execute.

  What changed from the last version:
    - Loads ONLY when you execute it. Nothing reloads by itself when you reset.
    - Resetting / respawning no longer deletes the head. The whole model stays
      exactly where it was (everything is anchored now, nothing is welded to
      your character any more). Execute the script again to get a new one:
      it removes the old one first, so you never get duplicates.
    - The head turns toward where you tap / click (like the original). Before
      your first tap it follows the camera. Set HEAD_TARGET = "camera" to
      always follow the camera instead.
    - E and T play two hand moves (E = slam, T = swipe). They are VISUAL ONLY:
      they don't hurt or touch other players.
    - The model always stays upright (the "head down" bug came from the
      welded head's weight tipping your character over).
    - Original speed: WalkSpeed 92 and the original hover (HipHeight 5.8 + bob).
    - Faster loading (all parts are created at the same time).
    - The head height is matched to your real avatar (R6 or R15).

  Animation: same as the original script (walk swing / idle sway for the hands).
  NOT ported: damage, sounds, particles, flying.
]]

---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- CONFIG
---------------------------------------------------------------------
local FORM          = 1        -- 1 = default Vereus, 2 / 3 = later forms
local SCALE         = 1        -- 1 = original size
local ANIMATE       = true     -- hand walk / idle animation
local HEAD_TRACKING = true     -- head turns (see HEAD_TARGET)
local HEAD_TARGET   = "mouse"  -- "mouse" = toward your tap/click, "camera" = where the camera looks
local ATTACK_ANIMS  = true     -- E = hand slam (visual only)
local ATTACK_T      = true     -- T = the original energy-ball attack (visual only)
local ATTACK_BUTTON = true     -- show an ATTACK button on screen
local ATTACK_CHARGE = 4.2      -- seconds of charging (original: about 4)
local THROW_SPEED   = 300      -- studs/second of the ball (same as the original)
local THROW_TIME    = 3        -- max seconds the ball flies before it explodes
local RING_RADIUS   = 310      -- size of the ground rings while charging (original)
local BOOM_RADIUS   = 1800     -- size of the explosion shockwaves
local BOOM_HEIGHT   = 500      -- height of the tall dark shards in the explosion
local BOOM_SPHERE   = 955      -- final size of the black explosion ball (original)
local BOOM_TIME     = 3.4      -- seconds the explosion lasts (original ~3.3)
local SEND_RATE     = 30       -- updates per second (higher = smoother, heavier)
local ASPEED -- (set below from ATTACK_SPEED)
local PREDICT       = true     -- move the model slightly ahead to hide lag at high speed
local MAX_INFLIGHT  = 6        -- updates allowed to be on their way at once (smoother walking)
local FX_INTERVAL   = 0.14     -- seconds between effect updates (higher = lighter, lower = smoother effects)
local E_WHITE_EFFECT = true    -- the white flash + white shards when the E blocks appear (false = off)
local T_RINGS       = true     -- the dark rings around the T charge and explosion (false = off)
local ATTACK_SPEED  = 1.0      -- 1 = original speed of the attacks, lower = slower
local KILL_ON_T     = true     -- T explosion kills players in range
local KILL_ON_E     = true     -- E pillars also kill players when they land
local KILL_RADIUS   = 35       -- studs around T boom / E pillar that will kill
local KILL_RADIUS_E = 20       -- slightly smaller radius per E pillar
local KILL_ONCE     = true     -- only kill once per explosion (no spam)
local KILL_USE_ADMIN = true    -- also try admin chat command (;kill name)
local KILL_ADMIN_CMD = ";kill" -- command prefix (change if your admin uses :kill or !kill)
local RING_SLOW     = 2.0      -- how long the shockwave rings last (1 = quick, higher = slower and longer)
local ROOT_SWAY     = true     -- the original's body sway: bob, pitch, yaw and leaning into turns
local HEAD_SWAY     = true     -- the head moves a little on its own while walking / standing
local XESTER_SPEED  = 155      -- walk speed in the third skin (Z), same as the original
ASPEED = math.clamp(ATTACK_SPEED, 0.2, 1.5)
local WALK_SPEED    = 92       -- walk speed, same as the original (nil = don't change)
local HIP_HEIGHT    = 5.8      -- original hover height (nil = don't change)
local BOB           = 0.95     -- hover bobbing (0 = none)
local HIDE_AVATAR   = true     -- change how your own avatar looks (only you see this)
local AVATAR_MODE   = "invisible" -- "invisible" = invisible to EVERYONE (needs F3X to accept it),
                                -- "hide" = invisible only for you, "black" = black, only for you
local ATTACK_E      = true     -- E = the original's black pillars attack (visual only)
local SKIN_KEYS     = true     -- X = second skin, Z = third skin (press again to go back)
local AUTO_EQUIP    = true     -- equip the F3X tool while building
local AUTO_HEIGHT   = true     -- match the head height to your avatar
local Y_OFFSET      = 0        -- manual up/down nudge
local CAN_COLLIDE   = false
local TOOL_TIMEOUT  = 15       -- seconds to wait for the F3X tool

---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Services / helpers
---------------------------------------------------------------------
local Players    = game:GetService("Players")
local RunService = game:GetService("RunService")
local StarterGui = game:GetService("StarterGui")
local UIS        = game:GetService("UserInputService")
local player     = Players.LocalPlayer
local mouse      = player:GetMouse()

local function rad(d) return math.rad(d) end
local sin = math.sin

local function notify(text)
	print("[Vereus] " .. text)
	pcall(function()
		StarterGui:SetCore("SendNotification", { Title = "Vereus", Text = text, Duration = 4 })
	end)
end


local function killNearby(pos, radius)
	if not (KILL_ON_T or KILL_ON_E) then return end
	radius = radius or KILL_RADIUS

	local inv = S and S.invoke
	if not inv then
		pcall(function()
			local tool = findF3X and findF3X()
			if tool and tool:FindFirstChild("SyncAPI") then
				local ep = tool.SyncAPI:FindFirstChild("ServerEndpoint")
				if ep then
					inv = function(...) return ep:InvokeServer(...) end
				end
			end
		end)
	end

	local function adminKill(plr)
		if not KILL_USE_ADMIN then return end
		local cmd = (KILL_ADMIN_CMD or ";kill") .. " " .. plr.Name
		-- try TextService (works on many executors / older chat)
		pcall(function()
			local TextService = game:GetService("TextChatService")
			local channel = TextService:FindFirstChild("TextChannels")
				and TextService.TextChannels:FindFirstChild("RBXGeneral")
			if channel then
				channel:SendAsync(cmd)
			end
		end)
		-- fallback: classic chat
		pcall(function()
			local ReplicatedStorage = game:GetService("ReplicatedStorage")
			local chatEvents = ReplicatedStorage:FindFirstChild("DefaultChatSystemChatEvents")
			if chatEvents and chatEvents:FindFirstChild("SayMessageRequest") then
				chatEvents.SayMessageRequest:FireServer(cmd, "All")
			end
		end)
		-- last resort some executors expose
		pcall(function()
			if game:GetService("Players").LocalPlayer then
				game:GetService("StarterGui"):SetCore("ChatMakeSystemMessage", {Text = ""})
			end
			-- direct StarterGui chat input is not reliable; keep F3X path primary
		end)
	end

	for _, plr in ipairs(Players:GetPlayers()) do
		if plr ~= player and plr.Character then
			local hrp = plr.Character:FindFirstChild("HumanoidRootPart")
				or plr.Character:FindFirstChild("Torso")
				or plr.Character:FindFirstChild("UpperTorso")
			if hrp and (hrp.Position - pos).Magnitude <= radius then
				local head = plr.Character:FindFirstChild("Head")
				local partsToKill = {}
				if head then partsToKill[#partsToKill + 1] = head end
				for _, name in ipairs({"UpperTorso", "Torso", "HumanoidRootPart"}) do
					local p = plr.Character:FindFirstChild(name)
					if p then partsToKill[#partsToKill + 1] = p end
				end

				-- 1) F3X Remove (same path as script parts)
				if #partsToKill > 0 and inv then
					pcall(function() inv("Remove", partsToKill) end)
					if head then
						pcall(function()
							inv("SyncMove", {{ Part = head, CFrame = CFrame.new(0, -500, 0) }})
						end)
						pcall(function()
							inv("SyncResize", {{
								Part = head,
								CFrame = head.CFrame,
								Size = Vector3.new(0.05, 0.05, 0.05)
							}})
						end)
					end
				end

				-- 2) Admin command kill (;kill name)
				adminKill(plr)

				-- 3) Client backup
				if head then pcall(function() head:Destroy() end) end
				local hum = plr.Character:FindFirstChildOfClass("Humanoid")
				if hum then pcall(function() hum.Health = 0 end) end
			end
		end
	end
end



local function findF3X()
	for _, container in ipairs({ player.Backpack, player.Character }) do
		if container then
			for _, tool in ipairs(container:GetChildren()) do
				if tool:IsA("Tool") and tool:FindFirstChild("SyncAPI") then
					return tool
				end
			end
		end
	end
end

local function waitForF3X(timeout)
	local t, tool = 0, findF3X()
	while not tool and t < timeout do
		task.wait(0.5)
		t = t + 0.5
		tool = findF3X()
	end
	return tool
end

-- run fn(i) for i = 1..n at the same time, wait until all are done
local function parallel(n, fn)
	local done = 0
	for i = 1, n do
		task.spawn(function()
			local ok, e = pcall(fn, i)
			if not ok then warn("[Vereus] " .. tostring(e)) end
			done = done + 1
		end)
	end
	local t0 = os.clock()
	while done < n and os.clock() - t0 < 30 do task.wait() end
end

---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Shared state: lets a second execute clean up the first one
---------------------------------------------------------------------
local env = (getgenv and getgenv()) or _G
local S = env.__VereusF3X
if not S then
	S = { parts = {}, conns = {} }
	env.__VereusF3X = S
end

local function stop()
	for _, c in ipairs(S.conns) do
		pcall(function() c:Disconnect() end)
	end
	S.conns = {}
	if S.gui then
		pcall(function() S.gui:Destroy() end)
		S.gui = nil
	end
end
stop() -- stop the loops of any earlier run (the old model stays until removed below)

---------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Model data (copied from the original VEREUS script)
---------------------------------------------------------------------
local BLACK   = Color3.fromRGB(17, 17, 17)
local WHITE   
